  "notes": "The research describes one group over two labels and says the two sound different, so this is authored as two modes rather than as their average. Bad Boy: replayed melodic bass, percussion layers, brighter. Ruff Ryders: Phrygian-flavoured synth-string motifs, a sustained sub on the tonic, dry, and the percussion layers stripped out. The base model sits between them on i–VI–VII and i–iv, which the research gives for both halves. ⚠ The sustained Ruff Ryders sub is `mirror_kick` at `followRootsProb` 0.95, not a held note — the engine's only note-holding bass rhythm emits one note per chord and saturates, so two low roots a bar over a kick on 1 and 3& is the nearest honest reading. ⚠ The bII in the ruff-ryders mode is INFERRED: the research says \"Phrygian-flavoured\" of the *motifs*, not of the chords, and this is the chord that phrase implies. It carries the lowest weight in that mode and is the first thing to delete. ⚠ `medium` because the research rates the entry medium-high and its numbers are label-sound level rather than session level.",
